# Optional debugging fragment — NOT part of a release kernel.
#
# Apply with:  HEMLOCK_KERNEL_EXTRA_CONFIG=debug-ll.config build-kernel.sh
# or by ticking `kernel_debug` on the image workflow.
#
# Why this exists: a kernel that dies before parse_early_param() has no
# console at all, so it fails identically to a kernel that was never
# entered — "Starting kernel ..." and then nothing, forever. earlycon
# cannot help, because earlycon is itself set up by parse_early_param.
# DEBUG_LL writes straight to the UART from head.S and from the zImage
# decompressor, before the MMU and before any console infrastructure
# exists, which is the only way to tell those two cases apart.
#
# Symbols below are taken from arch/arm/Kconfig.debug at v6.1, not
# guessed. Two traps in there worth recording:
#
#   * CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_8250 cannot be set by hand. It is
#     `def_bool ARCH_IOP32X || ARCH_IXP4XX || ARCH_RPC`, so it is only
#     ever acquired via `select` from a choice entry. Asserting it
#     directly is what made the first version of this file fail.
#
#   * DEBUG_BCM_HR2 is this SoC's own choice entry (it depends on
#     ARCH_BCM_HR2, which hemlock.config already sets, and it selects
#     DEBUG_UART_8250 and gives SHIFT=0 for free) — but it is named
#     "Hurricane 2 UART2" and its mainline defaults point at
#     0x18000400 / 0xf1000400, which is uart1. This board's console is
#     uart0 at 0x18000300 (bcm-hx4.dtsi: the APB bus maps 0x18000000
#     and uart0 sits at offset 0x300; ONIE and U-Boot both use it), so
#     the physical and virtual addresses are overridden below. The
#     0xf1000000 virtual window follows mainline's own iProc mapping.
CONFIG_DEBUG_LL=y
CONFIG_DEBUG_BCM_HR2=y
CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_PHYS=0x18000300
CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_VIRT=0xf1000300
CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_8250_SHIFT=0
CONFIG_EARLY_PRINTK=y
